<!--Post: 11968--><!--Time: 1111456772-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11968"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 5:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11968-->
<!--Post: 12005--><!--Time: 1111505902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12005"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 7:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I know I could never ever live there....no matter how much remodel...how many years.....poor Charlie...knowing it is still standing.<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/sad.gif" ALT=":-&#40;" BORDER=0> <BR>Makes me wonder if the people who purchased the home knew what had occurred there?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12005-->
<!--Post: 12014--><!--Time: 1111508196-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12014"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the residents are receptive, there has to be some wierd psychic stuff going on at the Otero home. There may be more calm since DR&#39;s capture, but I do agree that the &#39;ambience&#39; of the violent torture and death has to remain there. Should Charlie return there, some remarkable things/activities would occur. <BR> <BR>It would be interesting to trace the history of the house and see if anything violent or unearthly occured there prior to the Oteros taking up residence. I don&#39;t believe that full disclosure was required back then, and one could sell a lemon as sugar coated. I am always cautious of buying things that belonged to others because I don&#39;t know what those persons did or how they lived their lives. Just my personal wierdness.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12014-->
<!--Post: 12030--><!--Time: 1111514222-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If what you stated is &#34;your&#34; personal wierdness Teardrop....then it is &#34;mine&#34; also. <BR>I feel exactly the same way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12030-->
<!--Post: 12047--><!--Time: 1111533550-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12047"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 3:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Charlie said he plans to go back to the house, but the lady of the house said she probably won&#39;t let him in.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12047-->
<!--Post: 12109--><!--Time: 1111593078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12109"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 7:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would probably be cathartic for Charlie to face the demons of that horrible day by returning to the home. Surely the people of the house would let him into the home. They may be afraid that &#39;something&#39; would be stirred up by his presence. <BR> <BR>By the way, too many threads are being created. It is very difficult to follow them all. Must be my mentalpause.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12109-->
<!--Post: 12514--><!--Time: 1112331528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 8:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I drove by the Otero home today and the house numbers have been taken off...I have a feeling it&#39;s probably been that way for a long time, but it struck me...obviously very intentional...can&#39;t blame them.  There was also a paper on the door, I was dying to go read it, but I would never have the cahones to do that.  There was a guy in the backyard...the Otero&#39;s took much better care of the home than the people who live there now do. &#40;from what I can tell&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12514-->
<!--Post: 12515--><!--Time: 1112334614-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12515"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 9:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I live very close to the old Otero house. I see the people who now live there out and around quite often. I have never met them though. I did read, in the Wichita Eagle, an article about the family currently residing there. They DID NOT know of the house&#39;s previous past, they say. Although I thought when selling a house a realtor has to provide full disclosure. From what I read in the Eagle article, the husband is disabled and his wife is going to school and works part-time. I think it&#39;s hard for them to keep up on the repairs needed. I have seen the husband walking up and down our local neighborhood picking up trash thrown into the streets, trying to be a good neighbor. They did say in the article that they were of tired of the people driving by and staring, getting out of their cars and taking pictures, etc. I guess that&#39;s why I have not been too sympathetic with &#34;Rocky&#34; and his people over there on Rader&#39;s street. These people, &#40;the people living in the Otero house&#41;, did it the right way and went to the paper to make their requests POLITELY known. They are of the Morman faith and do not believe in ghosts or a lasting presence lurking around their home. From what they said in the article, they are reluctant to let Charlie Otero back into the home. She &#40;the wife&#41; said it&#39;s not the same house. It&#39;s been remodeled and the pipes in the basement are plastic, not the original pipes that would be in a house of that age. Most of these houses around here were built in the 40&#39;s. I completely understand Charlie O. wanting to go back. And I have to say, if it were my house, I&#39;d let him in. HIM ONLY. Who knows maybe she&#39;ll change her mind. <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12515-->
<!--Post: 12527--><!--Time: 1112365640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12527"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 6:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the police need to discover any info from Rader, it is &#39;why the Oteros?&#39;. If that was his initial venture as a serial killer, it is of great interest to know who was the target initially, and was that person secondary to causing pain to someone else. That is, was he planning to kill Julie to cause pain to Joe, etc. If that was his first homicide, Rader carried it off with the precision of a well versed murderer. <BR> <BR>Since her husband is disabled, perhaps the lady of the former Otero home &#40;for which it will ever be known&#41;, will understand the way Charlie has been disabled by the event in that house. I would discreetly request a change of house number from the city. I do believe in psychic phenomena, be it woman&#39;s intuition, a mother&#39;s sense that something is not right with her child, the way an animal shows an immediate distrust or liking of a person, a changed life through an encounter with God, and the resident evil of Dennis Rader. However, one cannot live in fear and trepidation of the dark side. There are many carryovers from superstitution, such as a mirror in the entryway of a home: to keep evil spirits out. Evidently, they don&#39;t like to look at themselves, and they will turn away. I wonder how much time Rader spent in front of the mirror, and what did he see. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12527-->
<!--Post: 12540--><!--Time: 1112398387-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12540"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 3:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, I agree the Why the Otero&#39;s is a big question and I have never been comfortable with the idea of which one was the intended victim. <BR>It seems to me that the whole family were intended victims and if not, and if he didn&#39;t expect Joe Otero to return home or that two of the kids would be there then why bring so much rope to the murder scene? <BR>Joe Sr., Joe Jr. and Julie Otero were bound around the neck, wrist and ankle areas while Josephine was bound around the neck and hung, bound around the upper torso, around the waist, above the knees and around the ankles. <BR>The ropes used on the victims were said to be well-worn venetian blind rope that wasn&#39;t from the otero house but was brought there by the killer. <BR>If he only planned on killing and binding one or two victims then why all the excess rope?  <BR>He actually had enough rope with him to use on a couple more victims since he used an excessive amount on Josephine. <BR>The whole crime scene of the Otero house doesn&#39;t look like the work of a first-time killer or the work of a solo killer to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12540-->
<!--Post: 12553--><!--Time: 1112419397-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12553"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From the comments of those who knew him, he always took more that most people took for a planned occassion. They stated that he was always prepared for almost any scenario. I wonder if they found his &#39;kit&#39; and its contents. Even if he carried all that stuff with him he could justify it. <BR> <BR>I was always amazed that Richard Speck could kill 8 women, all in the same room, and not have at least one of them hit him with a lamp, iron, whatever. The one that survived hid under a bed. Hopefully, Rader will be thoroughly debriefed on each homicide if he makes a plea. It would be very risky to have a partner because in a weak moment one would snitch on the other. He is such an egotistical fruitcake that I cannot see him sharing the limelight and glory with anyone else. <BR> <BR>A thorough look at his associates &#40;work, personal, etc.&#41; and deaths of those people that might have occurred shortly after the Otero deaths might lend light as to an accomplice. He surely would have bumped them off with a different MO and signature or an &#39;accident&#39;. Or he could have chosen a crazy person whom no one would have believed. The scenarios are endless. I do agree that the Oteros were no ordinary family in terms of self defense capability. But a split second of &#39;this cannot be happening to me&#39; can contribute to a assailant getting the upper hand. Only Turdbreath knows the answer. Another explanation is that Rader claimed credit for the Otero deaths after learning the facts from the actual killer and then rendered him dead, disabled, or not believable. However, his letter to the police contained such detail.  <BR> <BR>I hate that I did not print out the Charlie interview that I found on the KMBZ radio site. I found it in the cached part and it is not available now. That interview was the one in which Charlie stated that the FBI file indicated that at some point during the ordeal, his father was untied and made to write a letter or note. There lies the key, I would think. What in the world could have been in that note?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12553-->
<!--Post: 12557--><!--Time: 1112421842-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12557"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 10:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What is the rule on this: If they were to get a house mover to, say, move the Otero&#39;s house across the street, and move the one across the street to where the Oteros is, which one would be haunted? <BR> <BR>It seems that most informed sources, whether they admit it publicly or not, believe that the Otero&#39;s in general were the intended target and that whoever was home would be killed &#40;BTK[&amp;co.]may have been originally planning to wait around for the whole family, or they may have known Joe had an appointment [it might have been with one of them/him] and planned to kill Julie and wait for JoeI, then surprise him&#41;. <BR> <BR>The ultra-violence was intended as a warning to others&#40;?&#41;&#40;see columbian necktie&#41;.  <BR> <BR>The whole thing had been planned to happen differently, but things went awry&#40;?&#41;. <BR> <BR>Josephine Otero was almost as tall as Btk&#40;!&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12557-->
<!--Post: 12560--><!--Time: 1112422887-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12560"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 10:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Speck had a liitle practice before the murders of the student nurses and a little luck carrying them out.  <BR>Before moving to Illinois he was arrested 37 times in Dallas for public drunkeness, disorderly conduct, burglary and assault. Prior to his Chicago massacre of the nurses he had killed a barmaid, raped and robbed a 65 year old woman and was seen in an area where three girls dissappeared whose bodies were never found. <BR>The six nurses in the house were all sleeping when he barged in the house with a pistol and a knife and rounded them up from their beds, tied them up in one room and waited for the other three to come home one by one and tied them up too. With all victims bound he killed them one at a time. <BR>So as Teardrop points out it is possible to get the drop on a group of people with just a gun and a knife. Plus Speck did it while he was drunk and high while BTK most likely would have had sobriety working in his favor to accomplish his roundup of victims and murder. <BR>But Speck had a lengthy criminal record and murdered once and was suspected in the dissappeaance of three others along with rape and assault before his student nurse killings. Speck graduated to those killings but Dennis rader suspected as BTK had no criminal record and no known murder victims befor the Otero&#39;s. How does somebody get to that level who&#39;s never killed before? And in broad daylight. <BR>Speck&#39;s student nurse rampage was his undoing. Btk&#39;s Otero rampage was his begining. <BR>I can&#39;t believe the otero&#39;s were his first.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12560-->
<!--Post: 12564--><!--Time: 1112426559-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12564"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 11:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beatties book says, in an interview with one of Denny&#39;s buddies, that Rader frequently got roarin&#39; drunk &#40;pg 318&#41;. He also went to strip clubs. <BR> <BR>There was a 6-pack of empty cans found at Nancy Fox&#39;s-and she didn&#39;t drink. <BR> <BR>And here we were all thinking that he was a clean-living serial killer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12564-->
<!--Post: 12566--><!--Time: 1112440993-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12566"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 3:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read that told you he had a dark side, the bondage thing is still in question and i bet when he drank he was really mean.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12566-->
<!--Post: 12568--><!--Time: 1112463654-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12568"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 9:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My mention of Speck was more to the women and their lack of an organized or inidvidual response. Beattie&#39;s book came out here on the first. I have found some contradictions from what Charlie reported and the condition of the bodies at the Otero home. With Mr. Otero&#39;s boxing and combat training, I cannot believe that he would allow himself to be tied. It is a death sentence for sure. I still cannot conceive of all being dead as early 8:45 am, even if he did a blitz attack. This is all just so wretchedly heartbreaking. If Rader stayed until past 10am with the bodies, he was with Josephine. <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t you know that his wife could have smelled beer/alcohol/cigarette smoke on him? Could she have lived such a pristine life that she had never encountered the smell of beer? I do not see her ever returning to the Wichita area. There are almost as many questions for her as there are for her husband. No matter how secretive someone thinks they are being, someone who knew Rader&#39;s facade had to have seen him boozing and clubbing. And knowing him, they probably kept their mouths shut. I still wonder if he did not have bouts of impotence. There is no way he could have a normal sexual relationship with his wife and do the things that he did to Josie and other women. I beleve that bouts of impotency would enrage him and that may have sparked some of his killings, as he took it out on those whom he perceived as the cause of his lack of manly capabilities: women. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12568-->
<!--Post: 12571--><!--Time: 1112464689-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12571"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 9:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if when he got really drunk if he didn&#39;t get talkative also...hense some of the sloppier shootings and stabbings found along the road &#40;As he started to sober back up&#41;. <BR> <BR>Can you imagine how far off &#34;normal&#34; he would be with a snootfull. He could give Odie Hussin &#40;or whatever&#41; &#34;evil behavior lessons&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12571-->
<!--Post: 12599--><!--Time: 1112517005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12599"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 03, 2005 - 12:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was suprised to learn from Bmodule&#39;s post of Dennis Rader frequently geting really drunk and frequenting bars and strip clubs. I was a bartender for five years and I learned a lot of things from the drunken mouths of my customers about their lives and secrets. Rader must have been really careful to never reveal himself as BTK in any way or if he tripped up a little bit nobody ever caught on.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12599-->
<!--Post: 12624--><!--Time: 1112619752-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12624"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 6:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alot of people will say things when they are drunk that they are afraid to say when they are sober: it is a path to the truth for everyone. I am surprised that Rader would put himself in a compromising position; however, one thing that he has exhibited is self control to avoid detection. I bet he opened up about women, his mother, his wife, and things that he resented. Perhaps if his fellow drinkers and the bartenders look back, some of the things that he said add up in hindsight. I am surprised that his buddy was not questioned as to what he specifically did and said during those times of fellowship with BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12624-->
